{{!< default}}
{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     docs.hbs — the /docs/ index. Composed, because NSDS has no listing
     archetype for documentation: templates/docs.html is the ARTICLE
     (nav | article | outline), not the index that points at them.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     ⚠ SAME SILENT FALLBACK AS courses.hbs. The live routes.yaml has mounted
     /docs/ with `template: docs` since the previous port, and with no such
     file Ghost has been serving the blog grid instead — .ns-bcard covers and
     reading times over what are meant to be reference sections.

     ── WHY A TREE PER SECTION AND NOT A CARD GRID ──────────────────────────
     A card grid answers "which of these looks interesting", which is the
     blog's question. Documentation is arrived at to FIND something specific,
     so the index has to show what is INSIDE each section, not just that the
     section exists — otherwise every lookup costs two page loads.
     NSDS's .ns-tree is exactly this control, it is already vendored, and as
     a native <details> it needs no JavaScript: open/closed state, keyboard
     operation and in-page find all come from the platform.

     THE COUNT AND THE PAGES ARE BOTH COUNTED, NEVER TYPED — the same
     {{#get}} discipline as training/modules.hbs, leaning on THE ONE RULE
     from routes.yaml: a section post's slug equals its own tag's slug, which
     is what makes /docs/{section}/ and /docs/{section}/{page}/ line up.

     ⚠ limit is a NUMBER, never "all" — Ghost's {{#get}} does not support it.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<section class="ns-band ns-band--tight">
    <div class="ns-band__inner">
        <div class="ns-band__head ns-band__head--between">
            <div>
                <span class="ns-kicker">{{t "// Reference"}}</span>
                <h1 class="ns-band__title">{{t "Documentation"}}</h1>
                <p class="ns-band__lede">{{t "How the platform, the courses and your account work — the answers that do not change week to week."}}</p>
            </div>
            <div class="ns-band__actions">
                <a class="ns-btn ns-btn--outline ns-btn--sm" href="{{@site.url}}/training/">{{> "icons/graduation-cap"}} {{t "Training"}}</a>
            </div>
        </div>

        {{#if posts}}
            <div class="ns-blog-grid">
                {{#foreach posts}}
                    <article class="ns-card">
                        <div class="ns-card__body">
                            <span class="ns-card__kicker">{{t "// Section"}}</span>
                            <a class="ns-card__link" href="{{url}}"><h2 class="ns-card__title">{{title}}</h2></a>
                            {{#if excerpt}}<p class="ns-card__text">{{excerpt words="20"}}</p>{{/if}}

                            {{!-- The section's own pages, so a lookup lands in one
                                 click rather than two. `../` climbs out of the
                                 {{#get}} frame back to the section post. --}}
                            {{#get "posts" filter="primary_tag:{{slug}}+tag:hash-docs-page" order="published_at asc" limit="50" as |pages|}}
                                {{#if pages}}
                                    <ul class="ns-tree">
                                        {{#foreach pages}}
                                            <li><a class="ns-tree__node" href="{{url}}"><span class="ns-tree__label">{{title}}</span></a></li>
                                        {{/foreach}}
                                    </ul>
                                {{/if}}
                            {{/get}}
                        </div>
                    </article>
                {{/foreach}}
            </div>
            {{> "pagination"}}
        {{else}}
            {{> "empty" title=(t "No documentation yet")
                        text=(t "Reference material is being written.")}}
        {{/if}}
    </div>
</section>
